Vowelboard is a bilingual phonics toy: five sensor zones, one per vowel (A/E/I/O/U), each triggering a spoken vowel sound through a speaker. A language button toggles between English and Spanish audio sets, a volume switch sets loud/quiet, and the board runs on battery with low-battery detection.

The prototype was developed for an investor pitch and further details of the final client cannot be disclosed.

**Note** : This product was a part of the "PROOFin10" service where we work with clients to transform their ideas (..or claude chats) into actual physical products in 3 weeks with €10k of client investment. The final outputs are website, functional and scalable physical prototype, and pitch deck.
